# Rust
native/target/
# native/Cargo.lock IS committed (deliberately un-ignored during the monty 0.19
# upgrade). Cargo's "libraries don't commit lockfiles" convention does not apply
# here: hook/build.dart compiles this crate as a TOP-LEVEL package on every
# consumer's `pub get`, so it behaves like an application and the lockfile is
# honoured. Without it every consumer re-resolves transitively and can get a
# broken tree — which happened for real: fresh resolution picked get-size2
# 0.10.3, whose GetSize impl targets a different compact_str major than
# ruff_python_ast 0.0.3 uses, so the build failed with an unsatisfied trait
# bound in a dependency we do not control. Upstream monty pins get-size2 0.10.1
# in its own committed lockfile and builds fine.

# JS bridge build deps
js/node_modules/

# DCM local config contains credentials — never commit
.dcm.yaml

# assets/ JS/WASM files ARE committed to git (Mode A asset distribution).
# Regenerate with: bash tool/prebuild.sh
# CI verifies no drift on every PR.

